            mechanism: "Corticosteroids reduce edema in the compressed cord and can ease pain, buying time; they do not remove the tumor. Surgery removes the compressing mass at once and can stabilize a collapsing vertebra. Radiotherapy shrinks sensitive tumors over days.",
